{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"rg -n 'federated|manifest|pin' .pose/knowledge --glob '*.md' --max-count 1 | head -25; cat .pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md; rg --files .pose/rules | rg 'go|backend'; nl -ba pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go | sed -n '4710,4800p'; rg -n 'federated|closed.scope' pose-mcp/internal/cli/testdata/adversarial/README.md\"","aggregated_output":".pose/knowledge/archive/2026-09-24-handoff-multirepo-review-continuation.md:22:The Harne8 adoption fixture exercises the pinned old binary as well as the\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-07-19-handoff-contract-baseline-handoff.md:25:imutável digest-pinned, aprovação exige Execution Identity, `HarnessExecutor`\n.pose/knowledge/archive/2026-08-13-decision-log-install-one-liner-safe-form.md:27:   (spec pose-public-install-contract) pinned the exact pipe string as a\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-agency-readiness-outcome-review.md:47:  gaps and validate-native flapping by 2026-12-02, or sooner if relied on for a\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-sealed-review-bundles-review.md:20:The current full-body review scope digest lets closeout bookkeeping alter the\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-16-decision-log-module-metadata-discovery-invalidates-review-provenance.md:75:@pose-maintainers — no active handoff; revisit only if the digest-scoping\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-20-handoff-pose-b07-implementation.md:34:2. The unused expired Actions waiver was removed separately in d957b4f. No pin or enforcement change. Reconciled full suite, 11/11 mutations and native 141/141 validation passed before the latest three review fixes; regenerate final evidence at the configured .pose/results/delivery-validation.json.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-26-handoff-delegation-observation-round4.md:28:- F-R3-02 (low, graded medium in round 3 and lowered because the hand-back now precedes the agent, which leaves a window of about 100ms or a supervisor hung over 30s; the engine accepts only low as accepted risk): the SIGTERM, 30s grace and SIGKILL path of a stopped supervisor has no test (swapping SIGTERM for SIGKILL keeps the delegate suites green), and the SIGKILL fallback on the supervisor group does not reach the agent's own group.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-action-answer-proof-and-historical-time.md:22:Verify proof and request/answer bindings in the domain reader and reject invalid evidence before deriving satisfaction. Reuse the issuer verifier with explicit write time and recorded acceptance precision on reads. Keep current issuer pins/grants as the existing revocation boundary. Preserve SSH journal-only verification after registered-key rotation.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-11-02-handoff-roadmap-v7-independent-outcomes-20261102.md:34:f1 is quoted output drift; runtime qualifies key presence assertions and refuses unsigned MCP answers. No physical hardware or human identity guarantee is inferred. f2 leaves automated outcome evidence dependent on explicit independent judgment. Generic integration assessment has 64 unobserved consumers; two pre-existing invalid spec inputs leave technical-debt scan incomplete. Recurrence reports validate-native flapping but zero flagged failure clusters. These broad observations do not invalidate the freshly exercised roadmap paths.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-09-12-note-cli-output-design-taxonomy.md:61:- No TTY detection, no terminal-width or wrapping logic, no `--quiet`, no\n.pose/knowledge/README.md:17:- Liste vencidos: `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired`\n.pose/knowledge/2026-10-13-decision-log-review-assurance-requires-cryptographic-proof.md:26:Direct disclosure, verify, review-check, closeout and attribution consume the same authority proof check. Invalid proof never yields a verified claim that could authenticate human confirmation. No records, policy, schema or capability adoption are rewritten. Current issuer pins/grants and current expiry semantics remain; historical trust and reuse provenance require the separate B04 delta.\n.pose/knowledge/2026-08-13-decision-log-adr-component-aware-review-plans-review.md:42:invalidate approvals. Keep mapping provenance visible, include only consumed\n# Rule: Knowledge Governance\n\n## When to consult\n\nConsult this guide when creating, updating, reviewing, or removing artifacts under `.pose/knowledge/`.\n\n## TTL and retention\n\n- Set `expires_at` on every artifact when it is created.\n- Use a default TTL of 30 days for notes, decision logs, and handoffs.\n- Use a TTL of up to 90 days only with a justification recorded in the artifact body.\n- Treat an artifact without `expires_at` as non-compliant and block its creation or merge.\n\n## When this is not the right home\n\n- Use `.pose/knowledge/` only for time-bound operational memory: content\n  tied to a decision moment, a handoff between executions, or something\n  meant to be reviewed and eventually expire.\n- A durable fact or convention that will not become false and carries no\n  review trigger — a third-party tool's parsing quirk, a naming\n  convention, a recurring gotcha — is not a `decision-log` just because no\n  better type exists. Route it to `.pose/rules/` instead: add it to an\n  existing rule file or create one, then wire it into the relevant task\n  type's base `rules` array in `.pose/indexes/task-map.json` so\n  `pose suggest <task>` surfaces it automatically. No path scoping is\n  required — a task type's base `rules` list is returned regardless of\n  `--path`; only language/component-specific rules need the\n  `rules_by_domain` layer.\n- Rule of thumb: if nothing was decided or traded off, and nothing about\n  the fact will change on a predictable timeline, it is not a\n  `decision-log` and not an ADR — it is a rule. See ADR\n  `2026-08-15-durable-non-architectural-knowledge-belongs-in-rules-not-a-new-type`.\n\n## Reusable cross-execution format\n\n- Structure reusable context as a handoff with fixed sections: Context, Current state, Next checks, Risks, and Next owner.\n- Keep `source_refs` linked to the relevant spec, workflow, and executed check commands.\n- Record `last_reviewed_at` in the body to make effective cross-execution updates traceable.\n\n## Archiving and purging\n\n- Run biweekly triage to list expired artifacts.\n- Move expired artifacts to `.pose/knowledge/archive/` when they retain audit value.\n- Purge archived artifacts 180 days after expiration unless documented legal or compliance requirements apply.\n- Record every archive and purge action in the housekeeping log.\n\n## Sensitive content\n\n- Prohibit secrets, tokens, credentials, private keys, and equivalent material.\n- Prohibit personal data and non-anonymized customer data.\n- Do not copy restricted incidents or reports in full; keep only a controlled reference.\n- Classify frontmatter `sensitivity` as `public-internal` or `restricted`.\n- Remove identified sensitive content immediately and open a security follow-up.\n\n## Ownership and review\n\n- Keep `@pose-maintainers` as the primary governance owner.\n- Require an owner in every artifact frontmatter.\n- Review expiration biweekly and quality monthly.\n- Escalate a backlog overdue by more than two cycles to the primary owner.\n- Block backlog growth when `list-expired` exceeds the operational limit: zero in strict mode, two in tolerant mode.\n\n## Minimum operational checks\n\n- Run `pose knowledge-check --strict` biweekly to validate the expired backlog.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping list-expired` for detailed triage.\n- Run `pose knowledge-housekeeping archive-expired --dry-run` before applying changes.\n- Execute destructive actions only with an explicit `--apply` flag.\n.pose/rules/backend-go.md\n.pose/rules/knowledge-governance.md\n  4710\t// externalCommitmentUnchanged reads a spec dependency of another project at\n  4711\t// the sealed and the current revision, in that project's repository, and\n  4712\t// reports whether everything before its Final Report is the same: intent,\n  4713\t// requirements, plan, decisions and validation. Only the Final Report, where\n  4714\t// follow-ups are disposed, may differ. A plan digest covers the review\n  4715\t// procedure, not the requirements, so it cannot prove this (review round 1,\n  4716\t// F1). Anything that cannot be read is a change.\n  4717\tfunc (s Store) externalCommitmentUnchanged(then, now FederatedDependency) bool {\n  4718\t\tif now.Identity.Kind != \"spec\" || s.FederatedResolver == nil || s.FederatedResolver.Roots == nil || !isGitRevision(then.SourceRevision) || !isGitRevision(now.SourceRevision) {\n  4719\t\t\treturn false\n  4720\t\t}\n  4721\t\tsource, err := s.FederatedResolver.Roots.StoreFor(now.Identity.Project)\n  4722\t\tif err != nil {\n  4723\t\t\treturn false\n  4724\t\t}\n  4725\t\tspec, err := source.GetSpec(now.Identity.Slug)\n  4726\t\tif err != nil {\n  4727\t\t\treturn false\n  4728\t\t}\n  4729\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(source.Root, spec.Path)\n  4730\t\tif err != nil || rel == \"..\" || strings.HasPrefix(rel, \"..\"+string(filepath.Separator)) {\n  4731\t\t\treturn false\n  4732\t\t}\n  4733\t\trel = filepath.ToSlash(rel)\n  4734\t\tfiles := s.fsys()\n  4735\t\t// read returns a path's bytes at a revision, whether the path is there,\n  4736\t\t// and whether Git answered.\n  4737\t\tread := func(revision, path string) ([]byte, bool, bool) {\n  4738\t\t\tif _, err := captureFederatedGit(files, source.Root, \"cat-file\", \"-e\", revision+\":\"+path); err != nil {\n  4739\t\t\t\treturn nil, false, true\n  4740\t\t\t}\n  4741\t\t\traw, err := captureFederatedGit(files, source.Root, \"show\", revision+\":\"+path)\n  4742\t\t\treturn raw, true, err == nil\n  4743\t\t}\n  4744\t\tif info, err := source.fsys().Stat(spec.Path); err == nil && info.IsDir() {\n  4745\t\t\t// A section-split spec: every section but the Final Report is its\n  4746\t\t\t// commitment, read file by file (review round 2, N3).\n  4747\t\t\tfor _, name := range splitSpecSectionFiles {\n  4748\t\t\t\tif name == \"final-report.md\" {\n  4749\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  4750\t\t\t\t}\n  4751\t\t\t\tpath := rel + \"/\" + name\n  4752\t\t\t\tbefore, presentBefore, okBefore := read(then.SourceRevision, path)\n  4753\t\t\t\tafter, presentAfter, okAfter := read(now.SourceRevision, path)\n  4754\t\t\t\tif !okBefore || !okAfter || presentBefore != presentAfter || !bytes.Equal(before, after) {\n  4755\t\t\t\t\treturn false\n  4756\t\t\t\t}\n  4757\t\t\t}\n  4758\t\t\treturn true\n  4759\t\t}\n  4760\t\tbefore, present, ok := read(then.SourceRevision, rel)\n  4761\t\tif !present || !ok {\n  4762\t\t\treturn false\n  4763\t\t}\n  4764\t\tafter, present, ok := read(now.SourceRevision, rel)\n  4765\t\tif !present || !ok {\n  4766\t\t\treturn false\n  4767\t\t}\n  4768\t\treturn bytes.Equal(specCommitment(before), specCommitment(after))\n  4769\t}\n  4770\t\n  4771\t// specFinalReportTitle names a spec's Final Report heading, in either locale.\n  4772\tvar specFinalReportTitle = regexp.MustCompile(`(?i)^(?:\\d+\\.\\s+)?(?:final report|relat[óo]rio final)$`)\n  4773\t\n  4774\t// specCommitment is a spec's text before its Final Report, or the whole text\n  4775\t// when it has none. The section is found in the document's CommonMark\n  4776\t// structure, so a heading shown in a code block is not a section, and a\n  4777\t// heading with CRLF line ends is one (review round 2, N1, N2).\n  4778\tfunc specCommitment(raw []byte) []byte {\n  4779\t\tdoc := goldmark.New().Parser().Parse(text.NewReader(raw))\n  4780\t\tfor node := doc.FirstChild(); node != nil; node = node.NextSibling() {\n  4781\t\t\theading, ok := node.(*ast.Heading)\n  4782\t\t\tif !ok || heading.Level != 2 || heading.Lines().Len() == 0 {\n  4783\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  4784\t\t\t}\n  4785\t\t\ttitle := strings.TrimSpace(string(heading.Lines().Value(raw)))\n  4786\t\t\tif !specFinalReportTitle.MatchString(title) {\n  4787\t\t\t\tcontinue\n  4788\t\t\t}\n  4789\t\t\tstart := heading.Lines().At(0).Start\n  4790\t\t\treturn raw[:bytes.LastIndexByte(raw[:start], '\\n')+1]\n  4791\t\t}\n  4792\t\treturn raw\n  4793\t}\n  4794\t\n  4795\t// externalDependencyStands reports whether a dependency of another project,\n  4796\t// accepted at a moved pin, is still the commitment a closed scope's reviewer\n  4797\t// accepted. Its revision, content, evidence and review may have moved with\n  4798\t// the pin; its identity, relationship, resolution, done status, plan and\n  4799\t// governing contracts may not, and the current manifest names no blocker of\n  4800\t// it.\n46:| `retained-child-skips-its-verification` | delegated | A milestone seals over a done member whose own review verification no longer retains its approval — revoked federated trust, lost history, a later negative review (`pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestRetainedChildFollowsItsVerification`, `pose/review_subject_later_removal_test.go:TestMilestoneSealRetainsADoneChildsApprovedReview`) | pose-review-subject-later-removal |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
